% Learnograph — shared project preamble
% Include at the top of every prompt: <include>context/project_preamble.prompt</include>

% ── Backend stack ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% Language   : Python 3.11, FastAPI, Pydantic v2
% Database   : Postgres via backend/db/postgres.py — stores DAG snapshots, node state,
%               and resource visit history
% Memory     : mem0 via backend/memory/mem0_client.py — stores learning state across sessions
%               All mem0 calls are async (asyncio.to_thread wrappers) with try/except for
%               graceful degradation when mem0 is unavailable.
% Orchestration: RocketRide via backend/orchestration/rocketride_client.py — agents publish/subscribe
%               to named pipeline events; no agent calls another agent's function directly.
%               Pipeline topology defined in learnograph.pipe (project root).
% Realtime   : WebSocket server at WS /ws — pushes node state changes to the React frontend
%               the moment an agent updates state

% ── Frontend stack (reference only — agents do not generate frontend code) ───
% React + Next.js App Router, main page at frontend/app/page.tsx
% DAG rendered with React Flow in frontend/components/DAGCanvas.tsx
%   - Nodes are positioned by topological depth (computeDepths()), same-depth nodes share a row
% Voice check UI in frontend/components/VoiceCheck.tsx (calls ElevenLabs)
% WebSocket client hook at frontend/hooks/useWebSocket.ts
%   - Returns { nodes, connected, refresh } — refresh() does an immediate HTTP fetch of
%     /api/dag/{sessionId}, used to update the UI right after a comprehension pass

% ── Chrome extension (reference only) ────────────────────────────────────────
% Manifest V3 — content scripts per active tab, no persistent background listener
% extension/content.js extracts page title, meta, and visible text → POST to /classify
% Rtrvr.ai is called server-side after /classify receives the URL, not in the extension itself

% ── RocketRide event map — the orchestration contract every agent must follow ──

% Event published    | Published by           | Subscribed by
% dag.generated      | routes/dag.py route    | enrich_node (handle_dag_generated)
% node.enriched      | enrich_node            | (terminal — pushes dag.updated to WebSocket)
% content.classified | classify_content       | regenerate_dag (handle_content_classified)
% dag.regenerated    | regenerate_dag         | (terminal — pushes dag.regenerated to WebSocket)
% node.mastered      | routes/comprehension.py| regenerate_dag (handle_node_mastered),
%                    | route, after pass       | but main.py broadcasts immediately from DB
%                    |                        | state BEFORE LLM regeneration starts
% resource.visited   | routes/resource_visit.py| (terminal — pushes dag.updated to WebSocket)

% Each agent publishes exactly one event on successful completion and zero events on failure.
% No agent subscribes to an event it does not need.
% No agent publishes an event outside this table.

% ── mem0 write path — owned by the API layer, not by any agent ───────────────
% generate_dag   reads mem0 (user profile)   — never writes
% regenerate_dag reads mem0 (full state)     — never writes
% The FastAPI route handler writes to mem0 after comprehension_check returns pass
% and the node status is updated to mastered in Postgres.

% ── node.mastered fast-path broadcast ────────────────────────────────────────
% When the /comprehension/score route gets a "pass" verdict:
%   1. update_node_status(mastered) in Postgres
%   2. unlock_eligible_nodes() — immediately unlocks dependants in Postgres
%   3. record_node_mastered() in mem0
%   4. publish node.mastered
% _on_node_mastered subscriber in main.py:
%   1. Reads fresh state from Postgres (already correct — no LLM needed)
%   2. Broadcasts dag.updated to all WebSocket clients IMMEDIATELY
%   3. Fires handle_node_mastered as a background asyncio.create_task() for LLM reordering

% ── Project-wide MUST NOT rules (apply to all agents) ────────────────────────
% MUST NOT hand-patch generated output — edit the prompt and regenerate
% MUST NOT hardcode node IDs or match logic in code
% MUST NOT log API keys, bearer tokens, or mem0 secrets
% MUST NOT call another agent's function directly — communicate only via RocketRide pipeline events
%   (see table above) and shared DAG state in Postgres

% ── DAG node schema — shared contract for all agents ─────────────────────────

DAGNode schema (Pydantic v2, defined in backend/models/dag.py):

{
  "id": "react-hooks",
  "title": "React Hooks",
  "description": "useState, useEffect, useContext — the three hooks that cover 90% of use cases",
  "prerequisites": ["react-components", "javascript-closures"],
  "difficulty": "beginner | intermediate | advanced",
  "estimated_hours": 3,
  "success_criteria": "What is the difference between useEffect and useLayoutEffect, and when would you choose each?",
  "status": "locked | available | seen | mastered",
  "resources": [],
  "completed_at": null,
  "triggering_content": null
}

Field rules:
- id: kebab-case slug derived from the node title; must be unique within a DAG
- prerequisites: list of node IDs in the same slug-form; empty list means root node
- status transitions:
    locked → available  when all prerequisites are mastered (unlock_eligible_nodes or _normalize_statuses)
    available → seen    when the user visits any resource URL for this node (resource_visit route)
                        OR when content.classified matches this node (handle_content_classified)
    seen → mastered     when comprehension check passes (comprehension route)
- resources: populated by enrich_node; empty until that agent runs
  Resource.type values: "article" | "doc" | "youtube"
- completed_at: ISO-8601 timestamp; null until status transitions to mastered
- triggering_content: URL of the page that triggered the seen transition via content.classified; null otherwise

Request models (backend/models/dag.py):
- DAGGenerateRequest:  { topic: str, session_id: str }
- ClassifyRequest:     { page_url: str, session_id: str, page_text: str | None }
- ComprehensionRequest:{ node_id: str, success_criteria: str, transcribed_answer: str, session_id: str }
- ResourceVisitRequest:{ session_id: str, node_id: str, resource_url: str }
- RegenerateRequest:   { session_id: str }
